===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
[[File:04 Museum insect specimen drawer (Schmetterlings Exemplar) - Muzeum Gornoslaskie, Bytom, Poland.jpg|thumb|right|Museum stores its butterfly '''collection''' in special specimen drawers.]]

# A [[set]] of [[item]]s or amount of material [[procure]]d, [[gather]]ed or [[present]]ed together.
#: {{ux|en|The attic contains a remarkable '''collection''' of antiques, oddities, and random junk.}}
#: {{ux|en|The asteroid belt consists of a '''collection''' of dust, rubble, and minor planets.}}
#: {{ux|en|This year's Summer '''Collection''' will include a wide range of evening wear.}}
#: {{ux|en| He has a big '''collection''' of stamps.}}
#: {{ux|en|He has a superb coin '''collection'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=vii|text=Secondly, I continue to base my concepts on intensive study of a limited suite of '''collections''', rather than superficial study of every packet that comes to hand.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1837|author=w:William Whewell|title=History of the Inductive Sciences
|passage='''collections''' of moisture}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1887|author=Robert Bartholow|title=A Treatise on the Practice of Medicine
|passage=a purulent '''collection'''}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=5|passage=Of all the queer '''collections''' of humans outside of a crazy asylum, it seemed to me this sanitarium was the cup winner. {{...}} When you're well enough off so's you don't have to fret about anything but your heft or your diseases you begin to get queer, I suppose.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} A set of [[pitch]] classes used by a composer.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005| title=The Last Waltz of The Band |author=Neil Minturn | page=112| passage=The "collectional information" one receives is ambiguous since the '''collection''' { C, E, F, G, A } occurs in the key of C and in the key of F.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009| title=Musical Currents from the Left Coast |chapter=Form and Transpositional Combination in George Crumb's ''Lux Aeterna''|author=Brian Moseley|editor=Bruce Quaglia; Jack Boss | page=174| passage=In fact, students are often taught that specific '''collections'''—diatonic, octatonic, and whole-tone, etc.—typify these composers' compositional language.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012| title=Elliott Carter Studies |author=Marguerite Boland; John Link | page=22| passage=Simply put, the realm of available '''collections''' in a largely diatonic environment is much smaller than it is in truly ''atonal'' one. }}
# The [[activity]] of [[collect]]ing.
#: {{ux|en|'''Collection''' of trash will occur every Thursday.}}
# {{lb|en|set theory|topology|analysis}} A [[set]] of sets; ''used because such a thing is in general too large to comply with the formal definition of a set''.
# A gathering of money for charitable or other purposes, as by passing a contribution box for [[donation]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=7 Feb 76|volume=3|number=32|journal=Gay Community News|page=13|title=Playland: The Friendliest Place In Town|author=Rose Flower|quotee=Jimmy McGrath|text=The people here are very good to each other, too. When someone's house burned down, when someone was in the hospital, they took up '''collections''' for the people.}}
# {{lb|en|law}} [[debt collection|Debt collection]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The act of inferring or concluding from premises or observed facts; also, that which is inferred.
#* {{RQ:Milton Divorce|passage=We may safely say thus, that wrong '''collections''' have been hitherto made out of those words by modern divines.}}
# {{lb|en|UK}} The [[jurisdiction]] of a [[collector]] of [[excise]].
# {{lb|en|Oxon|usually|in the plural}} A set of [[college]] [[exam]]s generally taken at the start of the [[term]].
# The quality of being [[collected]]; [[calm]] [[composure]].

